// RUN: echo 'not real dxbc' > %t.dxbc
// RUN: not feme --target=dxil %t.dxbc -o %t.dxil 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

// `feme` auto-detects its input's format from its contents (see
// feme::detectFormat in feme/lib/Driver/Driver.cpp); it should reject
// input it cannot recognize as any supported format cleanly (a diagnostic
// and non-zero exit), not crash. This also covers legacy DXBC bytecode,
// which is not yet implemented (see the Roadmap / Milestones section of
// feme/docs/Design.md) and so cannot be distinguished from arbitrary
// unrecognized input.

// CHECK: feme: could not detect input file format
